    "title": "Who puts Rory McIlroy's green jacket on if he repeats as Masters champion? - Yahoo Sports",
    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTRENDINGNBA Play-In TournamentNFL mock draft 8.1LIV Golf's murky futureNBA Mock Draft 2.0MLB Power RankingsStory byBilly HeyenSun, April 12, 2026 at 5:17 PM CDT·1 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GoogleWho puts Rory McIlroy's green jacket on if he repeats as Masters champion? originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.Rory McIlroy is trying to become just the fourth golfer to repeat as Masters champion.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementIf he does it, it'll bring up a fascinating question that golf fans everywhere have begun to ask.The Green Jacket is the highlight of the Masters. It goes to the champion, an honor like no other in sports.Usually, the defending champ puts it on the new winner. What if the defending champion is the same guy?Who puts the green jacket on Rory McIlroy?Rory won't put the jacket on himself.Traditionally, the club chairman puts the jacket on the repeat champion.Augusta National's current chairman is Fred Riley. So that seems to be what will happen if McIlroy can hold on.Have there been back-to-back Masters champions?There have been three repeat Masters champs before the 2026 tournament.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementJack Nicklaus did it.Nick Faldo did it.And Tiger Woods did it.No one has ever done three in a row, but first, McIlroy is trying to make it two in a row and join an exclusive club.More Masters news:The wild cell phone rule at the MastersWhy Phil Mickelson is missing from the MastersHow Hojgaard golfers are relatedExplaining the history of Amen Corner at the MastersMeet the beloved Masters gnomeAdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
